ue_on":null,"closed_at":"2026-06-19T16:54:35Z"},"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-06-11T04:29:51Z","updated_at":"2026-06-16T17:51:55Z","closed_at":"2026-06-16T17:51:55Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.7.RC1, 4.7.Dev5\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.dev5 - SteamOS holo on Wayland - Wayland display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated AMD Custom GPU 0932 (RADV VANGOGH) - AMD Custom APU 0932 (8 threads) - 14.45 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\n\nWhen global illumination from a voxelGI node is calculated for an AreaLight3D with a large enough size (it seems to start at around 30m), part of the light doesn't receive any global illumination at all\n<img width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2eb9d113-24cb-44c6-91f4-9ce0c738b3c5\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a new 3D scene\n- Add one or two meshes for the light to shine onto\n- Add an AreaLight3D, extend one its sides out to 30-55 meters\n- Add a voxelGI that covers the entire scene\n- Bake the voxelGI\nThe MRP is a project with this setup\nWithin the MRP, you can toggle the VoxelGI node on and off to see that a portion of the light isn't affect at all\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[area-3d-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28822643/area-3d-bug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.gi